Description: Fix CVE-2026-48522 — reject non-http(s) JWKS URI schemes in PyJWKClient
 PyJWKClient previously passed its uri argument straight to urllib.request.urlopen,
 which uses Python's default OpenerDirector with FileHandler, FTPHandler and
 DataHandler registered. An attacker who could influence the URI (for example via
 a JWT `jku` header) could therefore coerce PyJWKClient into reading local files
 (file://), reaching FTP servers, or fetching data: URIs. This patch rejects any
 URI whose scheme is not "http" or "https" eagerly in PyJWKClient.__init__, and
 adds matching regression tests.
 .
 This is the CVE-minimal subset of upstream commit 95791b1 (which bundles five
 unrelated security fixes for the 2.13.0 release); only the scheme allowlist
 hunk and its tests are included here.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/95791b1759b8aa4f2203575d344d5c78564cdc81
Bug: https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4
Author: José Padilla <jpadilla@users.noreply.github.com>
Last-Update: 2026-06-30

